Wake a blocking default-context wait after completion on another thread.

The imported wait fix blocks instead of spinning. Its condition signal wakes
non-owner waiters, but cannot wake an owner blocked in the main context poll.
GLib main-context wakeup also covers that completion without changing the
result, finished flag, callback ownership, or QMI protocol.

--- a/src/libssc-common.c
+++ b/src/libssc-common.c
@@ -97,6 +97,7 @@
 	ctx->result = g_object_ref (result);
 	ctx->finished = TRUE;
 	g_cond_signal (&ctx->condition);
+	g_main_context_wakeup (g_main_context_default ());
 	g_mutex_unlock (&ctx->mutex);
 }
